ive tool for visualization of genomic variation</article-title><source>Nat Genet</source><year>2005</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>109</fpage><lpage>110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15678133</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/ng0205-109</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cotton</surname><given-names>RGH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Progress of the HUGO Mutation Database Initiative: a brief introduction to the <italic>Human Mutation </italic>MDI special issue</article-title><source>Human Mutation</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10612814</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1098-1004(200001)15:1&#x0003c;4::AID-HUMU3&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-T</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giardine</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Riemer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hefferon</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsu</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Zielenski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sang</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Elnitski</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cutting</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Trumbower</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>PhenCode: connecting ENCODE data with mutations and phenotype</article-title><source>Human Mutation</source><year>2007</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>554</fpage><lpage>562</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17326095</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/humu.20484</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citatio